[# promotional/countdown: a countdown block: a timer image, with the end time written out as text.

   Email clients do not run JavaScript, so a live ticking timer is impossible inside an email. The usual technique is
   an image URL served by an external countdown-timer service that draws the time left each time the email is opened.
   Pass that URL as `timerImage`. Without one this shows the end time as large text, which is the honest fallback:
   it is also what everyone sees when images are blocked. The image alt text always carries the end time.
   Check the service you use for how it caches images, some show the time from the first open.

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: a normal image (animated GIF timers show only their first frame in Outlook desktop).
   - Gmail apps: images load through Google's proxy, which can cache them, so a timer may show a stale time.
   - Dark mode: on the brand surface (light variant) text and background swap, on colored bands the colors stay. #]
[% set tn = tone(s) %]
[% set nodes = [] %]
[% if data.headline %][% set _ = nodes.push({ component: 'content/heading', data: { text: data.headline }, settings: { level: 'h2', tag: 'h2', align: s.align, color: tn.color, darkMode: tn.darkMode } }) %][% endif %]
[% if data.timerImage %]
[% set _ = nodes.push({ component: 'content/image', data: { image: { src: data.timerImage, alt: 'Offer ends ' + data.endsAt } }, settings: { align: s.align, padding: '0 0 @spacing.sm 0' } }) %]
[% set _ = nodes.push({ component: 'content/text', data: { text: 'Ends ' + data.endsAt }, settings: { level: 'bodySmall', align: s.align, color: tn.color, darkMode: tn.darkMode, padding: '0 0 @spacing.sm 0' } }) %]
[% else %]
[% set _ = nodes.push({ component: 'decorative/eyebrow', data: { text: s.label }, settings: { align: s.align, color: tn.color } }) %]
[% set _ = nodes.push({ component: 'content/heading', data: { text: data.endsAt }, settings: { level: 'h1', tag: 'div', align: s.align, color: tn.color, darkMode: tn.darkMode, padding: '0 0 @spacing.sm 0' } }) %]
[% endif %]
[% if data.cta %][% set _ = nodes.push({ component: 'content/button', data: data.cta, settings: { align: s.align, background: s.buttonBackground, color: s.buttonColor, darkMode: tn.buttonDark, padding: '@spacing.xs 0 0 0' } }) %][% endif %]
[[ c('layout/section', { content: nodes }, { settings: { background: s.background, padding: s.padding, hideOnMobile: s.hideOnMobile, hideOnDesktop: s.hideOnDesktop } }) ]]
